[ext_resource type="Texture2D" uid="uid://bkd1st34jky85" path="res://assets/themes/factory/conveyors/conveyor_split_42_v2.png" id="25_split"]

; Route geometry is derived from the conveyor artwork, not the other way round.
; Every corner is a circular fillet whose radius matches the centreline arc the
; bend/splitter art is drawn with, so a block stays on the belt centre through
; the turn instead of cutting it.
;
; Retuned for the v2 bend, measured off the PNG: its diagonal arm sits at
; 45.218 deg (v1 was 43.079) and its centreline arc radius is 455 tex px.
; Inbound diagonals therefore run at the art's own 45.218 deg.
;
; Outbound diagonals run at 43.726 deg, retuned again for the v2 splitter,
; whose branches measure 42.773 deg from vertical. That angle splits the
; residual between the splitter branch and the v2 bend arm (44.782 deg),
; holding both pieces within 1.8 px of the travelled line.

